WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.447
A reserve before it had finished forming, beside an island with twelve centuries of history.

00:00:06.547 --> 00:00:11.856
Surtsey was declared a nature reserve in 1965, two years before the eruption ended,

00:00:11.856 --> 00:00:16.398
and has been closed to everyone except permitted scientists ever since.

00:00:16.398 --> 00:00:19.852
No seeds, soil or living things may be carried ashore.

00:00:20.952 --> 00:00:25.528
Heimaey, the largest Westman Island, has been settled since the ninth century.

00:00:25.528 --> 00:00:27.640
On the twenty-third of January 1973,

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.981
a fissure opened at the edge of its town and built a new volcano, Eldfell.

00:00:31.981 --> 00:00:36.792
Nearly all of the town's roughly five thousand three hundred people were evacuated

00:00:36.792 --> 00:00:38.611
overnight by the fishing fleet.

00:00:39.711 --> 00:00:43.941
Crews pumped seawater onto the advancing lava to slow it and save the harbour.

00:00:43.941 --> 00:00:47.304
Today the new lava field stands right beside the rebuilt town.
